  "text": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c27b3ab3c8@example.invalid",
    "text": "<p><i>95% of Registered Eligible U.S. Patients Enrolled in Program</i></p>\n<p>Stryker Corporation (NYSE:SYK) announced that Howmedica Osteonics Corp. (referred to as &quot;Stryker Orthopaedics&quot;), a subsidiary of Stryker Corporation, has informed the courts in the New Jersey Multicounty and Federal Multidistrict litigations that 95% of additional registered eligible patients have enrolled in the Settlement Program under the Master Settlement Agreement announced in December 2016. As a result, Stryker Orthopaedics will move forward with the 2016 Settlement Program that provides for compensation to additional eligible U.S. patients who had surgery to replace their Rejuvenate Modular-Neck hip stem and/or ABG II Modular-Neck hip stem, known as a revision surgery, prior to December 19, 2016.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://investors.stryker.com/press-releases/news-details/2017/Stryker-Orthopaedics-2016-Settlement-Program-reaches-milestone/default.aspx\">Read the full release here</a>.&nbsp;</p>\n",
